{{begin-newsitem |time=2026-09-26T08:00:13Z |title=Chkdraft 2.15 released |author=Ojan |categories=StarCraft I, tools |summary=Chkdraft 2.15 is out with three changes}}

Yesterday, {{highlight |text=TheNitesWhoSay}} released version 2.15 of the StarCraft I map editor {{highlight |text=Chkdraft}}.

It is a smaller release with three changes:

- The submenu tools/scripts now has a script to downgrade maps from remastered
- Support for new cosmonarchy weapon limits
- Better logging/debugging/browsing when dat file loading has issues

Version 2.15 is available [here](https://github.com/TheNitesWhoSay/Chkdraft/releases/tag/2.15).
